:"உம்","lemma":"um","gloss":"also"}],"gloss":"his own self too"},{"surface":"தூக்கி","parts":[{"text":"தூக்கி","lemma":"tūkku","gloss":"considering/weighing"}],"gloss":"considering"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"இருங்கடறு","parts":[{"text":"இருமை","lemma":"irumai","gloss":"dark/great"},{"text":"கடறு","lemma":"kaṭaṟu","gloss":"forest"}],"gloss":"dark forest"},{"surface":"வளைஇய","parts":[{"text":"வளை","lemma":"vaḷai","gloss":"surround"},{"text":"இய","lemma":"iya","gloss":"adjectival participle suffix"}],"gloss":"surrounded"},{"surface":"குன்றத்","parts":[{"text":"குன்றத்","lemma":"குன்றத்","gloss":"of the hill"}],"gloss":"of the hill","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"தன்ன","parts":[{"text":"தன்ன","lemma":"தன்ன","gloss":"like"}],"gloss":"like","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"ஓர்","parts":[{"text":"ஓர்","lemma":"ōr","gloss":"one/a"}],"gloss":"a"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"பெருங்களிறு","parts":[{"text":"பெருமை","lemma":"perumai","gloss":"great/huge"},{"text":"களிறு","lemma":"kaḷiṟu","gloss":"male elephant"}],"gloss":"huge male elephant"},{"surface":"நல்கியோனே","parts":[{"text":"நல்கு","lemma":"nalku","gloss":"give"},{"text":"இ","lemma":"i","gloss":"past tense marker"},{"text":"ஓன்","lemma":"ōṉ","gloss":"he who did"},{"text":"ஏ","lemma":"ē","gloss":"emphasis"}],"gloss":"he gave indeed"},{"surface":"அன்னதோர்","parts":[{"text":"அன்னது","lemma":"aṉṉatu","gloss":"such a thing"},{"text":"ஓர்","lemma":"ōr","gloss":"one"}],"gloss":"such a"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"தேற்றா","parts":[{"text":"தேற்று","lemma":"tēṟṟu","gloss":"understand/clarify"},{"text":"ஆ","lemma":"ā","gloss":"negative relative participle"}],"gloss":"unreasoning/uncomprehending"},{"surface":"ஈகையும்","parts":[{"text":"ஈகை","lemma":"īkai","gloss":"generosity/giving"},{"text":"உம்","lemma":"um","gloss":"also"}],"gloss":"generosity also"},{"surface":"உளதுகொல்","parts":[{"text":"உளது","lemma":"uḷatu","gloss":"exists"},{"text":"கொல்","lemma":"kol","gloss":"particle of doubt"}],"gloss":"does it exist?"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"போற்றார்","parts":[{"text":"போற்று","lemma":"pōṟṟu","gloss":"limit/protect/cherish"},{"text":"ஆர்","lemma":"ār","gloss":"they (negative)"}],"gloss":"they do not limit"},{"surface":"அம்ம","parts":[{"text":"அம்ம","lemma":"amma","gloss":"alas"}],"gloss":"alas"},{"surface":"பெரியோர்","parts":[{"text":"பெரியோர்","lemma":"periyōr","gloss":"great people"}],"gloss":"great people"},{"surface":"தம்","parts":[{"text":"தம்","lemma":"tam","gloss":"their"}],"gloss":"their"},{"surface":"கடனே","parts":[{"text":"கடன்","lemma":"kaṭaṉ","gloss":"duty"},{"text":"ஏ","lemma":"ē","gloss":"emphasis"}],"gloss":"duty indeed"}]}],"literal":"The lord of Nāñcil hill with broad-standing jackfruit trees / is surely foolish, O poets of truthful tongues! / Plucked from the garden by bangle-wearing female dancers, / to be a side-dish for the greens, we, some / rice requested; since [we did so], he indeed, / knowing the worthiness [of us] and considering his own [status], / like a hill surrounded by a dark forest, a / huge male elephant gave! Such an / uncomprehending generosity, does it exist? / Alas, great people do not limit their duty!","translation":"O poets of truthful tongues! The lord of Nāñcil hill, where broad jackfruit trees stand, is surely foolish. When we asked for just a little rice to eat as a side-dish with the greens plucked from the garden by our bangle-wearing female dancers, he, considering our worthiness and his own status, gave us a huge male elephant that resembles a hill surrounded by a dark forest! Does such unreasoning generosity exist anywhere else? Alas, great people do not limit their duty!","modern":"பரந்த கிளைகளையுடைய பலா மரங்கள் நிறைந்த நாஞ்சில் மலையின் தலைவன், உண்மையான நாவினைக் கொண்ட புலவர்களே, நிச்சயமாக அறிவிலி ஆவான்! வளையல் அணிந்த கைகளை உடைய விறலியர் தோட்டத்தில் பறித்த கீரைக்குக் கூட்டாக உண்பதற்கு நாங்கள் சில அரிசியைக் கேட்டோம். ஆனால் அவனோ, எமது தகுதியையும் தனது தகுதியையும் ஆராய்ந்து பார்த்து, கரிய காடு சூழ்ந்த குன்றைப் போன்ற ஒரு பெரிய ஆண் யானையைப் பரிசாக அளித்தான்! இத்தகைய அளவற்ற கொடைத்தன்மை வேறு எங்கும் உண்டோ? பெரியோர்கள் தங்களது கடமையின் எல்லையைக் காக்க மாட்டார்கள் போலும்!","explanation":"This poem is composed by the famous poet Avvaiyār in praise of the chieftain Āy Aṇṭiraṉ, referred to here as the lord of Nāñcil hill. The poet addresses her fellow poets with a touch of loving irony, calling the chieftain 'foolish' for his excessive generosity. She explains that when her troupe of dancers gathered wild greens from the backyard and needed just a little rice to accompany the meal, they asked the king for rice. Instead of giving a small measure of grain, the king considered his own royal stature and the worthiness of the poets, and gifted them a massive war elephant, which looked like a forested hill. Avvaiyār marvels at this 'unreasoning' or 'uncalculating' generosity, concluding that truly great people do not limit or calculate their duty when it comes to giving.","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"},"timing":{"male":[[0.0,0.7],[0.7,1.2],[1.2,1.3],[1.3,1.7],[1.7,2.6],[2.6,2.7],[2.7,3.0],[3.0,3.7],[3.7,4.8],[4.8,5.0],[5.0,5.4],[5.4,5.8],[5.8,6.23],[6.23,6.88],[6.88,6.88],[6.88,7.5],[7.5,7.8],[7.8,8.9],[8.9,8.9],[8.9,8.9],[8.9,8.9],[8.9,8.9],[8.9,10.6],[10.6,11.0],[11.0,11.1],[11.1,11.6],[11.6,12.61],[12.9,13.3],[13.3,13.4],[13.85,14.0],[14.1,14.3],[14.3,15.0],[15.0,15.6],[15.6,16.1],[16.94,17.44],[17.64,18.04],[18.04,18.64],[18.64,19.44],[19.44,19.54],[19.54,20.14],[20.14,20.44],[20.44,20.74]],"female":[[0.0,0.7],[0.7,1.3],[1.3,1.5],[1.5,1.9],[1.9,3.2],[3.2,3.3],[3.3,3.6],[3.6,4.4],[4.4,5.8],[5.8,6.0],[6.0,6.5],[6.5,7.0],[7.0,7.38],[7.38,7.38],[7.38,7.38],[7.38,7.38],[7.38,7.38],[7.38,7.38],[7.38,8.92],[9.31,10.46],[10.46,12.0],[12.0,12.5],[12.5,12.9],[12.9,13.4],[13.4,13.5],[13.5,14.1],[14.1,14.1],[14.1,16.1],[16.1,16.2],[16.2,16.8],[16.93,17.07],[17.2,17.7],[17.7,18.5],[18.5,19.0],[19.8,20.4],[20.4,20.8],[20.8,21.5],[21.5,22.5],[22.5,22.6],[22.6,23.3],[23.3,23.5],[23.5,23.9]]}}